2026-09-17T00:34:51.4339710Z       "body": "### Summary\r\nWhen two routes use different Starlette path converters on the same path template (e.g. `{id:int}` and `{id:str}`), FastAPI's OpenAPI generator strips the converter suffix via `route.path_format`, causing both routes to normalize to the same key (e.g. `/items/{id}`).\r\n\r\nThe second route silently overwrites the first in the `paths` dict.\r\n\r\nThis means:\r\n- The **runtime router** (Starlette) matches the **first** registered route\r\n- The **OpenAPI spec** documents the **last** registered route\r\n- Swagger UI shows a handler that **cannot be reached at runtime**\r\n\r\nThis bug was reported in Discussion #15104 and a FastAPI collaborator confirmed it should be fixed.\r\n\r\n### Minimal repro\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\r\n\r\napp = FastAPI()\r\n\r\n@app.get(\"/items/{item_id:str}\")\r\ndef get_str(item_id: str):\r\n    return {\"id\": item_id}\r\n\r\n@app.get(\"/items/{item_id:int}\")\r\ndef get_int(item_id: int):\r\n    return {\"id\": item_id}\r\n\r\n# Runtime executes get_str (first match)\r\n# OpenAPI spec documents get_int (last registered) ← wrong\r\n```\r\n\r\n### What this PR does\r\n\r\n- **`fastapi/openapi/utils.py`**: adds a `warnings.warn()` in `get_openapi()` when a route (or webhook) would overwrite an existing OpenAPI path+method combination, with a message that names the colliding path and methods and explains the converter mismatch cause.\r\n\r\n- **`tests/test_openapi_path_converter_collision.py`**: regression tests covering collision detection, the no-collision case, and a case with same param name vs different param names.\r\n\r\n- **`docs/en/docs/tutorial/path-params.md`**: adds a note under the \"Order Matters\" section explaining that different path converters on the same path template collapse to the same OpenAPI path, and recommends using distinct parameter names.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n- [ ] The code change is tested and all existing tests pass\r\n- [ ] Tests covering the changes have been added\r\n- [ ] Docs have been updated where relevant\r\n- [ ] I have read the [Contributing Guide](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/contributing/)",
